<article class="env-lemma" id="08HR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08HR">Lemma <span data-tag="08HR">10.154.6</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map with $S$ henselian local. Given </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
an $R$-algebra $A$ which is a filtered colimit of étale $R$-algebras, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
a prime $\mathfrak q$ of $A$ lying over $\mathfrak p = R \cap \mathfrak m_ S$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
a $\kappa (\mathfrak p)$-algebra map $\tau : \kappa (\mathfrak q) \to S/\mathfrak m_ S$, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then there exists a unique homomorphism of $R$-algebras $f : A \to S$ such that $\mathfrak q = f^{-1}(\mathfrak m_ S)$ and $f \bmod \mathfrak q = \tau $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $A = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ i$ as a filtered colimit of étale $R$-algebras. Set $\mathfrak q_ i = A_ i \cap \mathfrak q$. We obtain $f_ i : A_ i \to S$ by applying Lemma <a href="/tag/08HQ" data-tag="08HQ">10.153.11</a>. Set $f = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits f_ i$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>